            <div xml:id="d78">

                <pb facs="0093" n="81" xml:id="pg81"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00113 European War 1939/545: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-11-07T23:00:00+01:00">November 7, 1942—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 8—1:13 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6268. Referring to Department’s 5213, October 22, 2 p.m., and Embassy’s 5422,
                    September 29, 10 p.m. The Foreign Office have accepted the Department’s
                    suggestion, Department’s 5213, October 22, 2 p.m., with reference to Soviet
                    participation in the declaration on property transfers in Axis dominated
                    territories. Eden, through Maisky, has invited Soviet participation in a
                    declaration modified on the lines suggested by the Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
